# Deny everything, then admit only what the build actually compiles.
#
# An allow-list rather than a deny-list because the things that must never enter
# a build context here are exactly the things nobody remembers to add: a
# tailscale auth key dropped in the working tree, a ./state directory holding a
# live node identity, a .env written during debugging. A missed deny-list entry
# bakes those into an image layer; a missed allow-list entry only breaks the
# build.
*

!go.mod
!go.sum
!cmd/
!internal/
!LICENSE

# .git stays excluded, which is why the build passes -buildvcs=false and takes
# the version as a build argument.
